---
import { Code } from "astro:components";
import fs from "node:fs";
import path from "node:path";
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import { cppSnippetDirectory } from "@/lib/technicalCabinet";

const filename = "blank-page-killer.cpp";
const source = fs.readFileSync(
  path.join(cppSnippetDirectory("project-start"), filename),
  "utf8",
);
---

<Layout
  title="The Blank Page Killer • C++ Cabinet"
  description="A C++ project-starting template that separates design ownership from reference work and turns progress into evidence."
>
  <article class="pb-14 pt-10">
    <div class="reading-copy prose prose-invert mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 md:px-0">
      <nav class="not-prose mb-8 font-mono text-sm">
        <a href="/cabinet/" class="text-[#5eead4] hover:text-[#c084fc]">
          ~/cabinet
        </a>
        <span class="text-white/35"> / </span>
        <a href="/cabinet/cpp/" class="text-[#5eead4] hover:text-[#c084fc]">
          cpp
        </a>
        <span class="text-white/35"> / project-start</span>
      </nav>

      <p
        class="not-prose font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-[#c084fc]"
      >
        Project-starting tool
      </p>
      <h1>The Blank Page Killer</h1>
      <p>
        This template does not design a program or write it for me. It turns a
        blank source file into a sequence of decisions: mission, smallest
        working version, inputs, outputs, data, flow, known tools, research
        boundaries, and the next observable checkpoint.
      </p>
      <p>
        Looking up syntax is part of programming. I still own the intent,
        architecture, data model, control flow, decisions, and understanding of
        the code I keep.
      </p>

      <div
        class="not-prose my-8 rounded-xl border border-[#5eead4]/25 bg-[#5eead4]/5 p-5"
      >
        <p class="m-0 font-mono text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/80">
          The goal is not “Can I write this entire program from memory?” The
          goal is “Do I know what I am trying to build, and can I work out how
          to build it?”
        </p>
      </div>

      <div
        class="not-prose mb-3 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 font-mono"
      >
        <h2 class="m-0 text-xl text-[#5eead4]">{filename}</h2>
        <a
          href={`/cabinet/cpp/project-start/${filename}`}
          class="text-xs text-[#c084fc] hover:text-white"
        >
          raw source ↗
        </a>
      </div>
      <Code code={source} lang="cpp" theme="github-dark" />
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
